/-!
# The moment map of the diagonal torus on the Riemann sphere

The Riemann sphere `OnePoint ℂ` is the complex projective line through Mathlib's
`OnePoint.equivProjectivization`, which sends `t` to `[t : 1]` and `∞` to `[1 : 0]`. The diagonal
torus acts on it by `(θ₀, θ₁) · [z₀ : z₁] = [e^{iθ₀} z₀ : e^{iθ₁} z₁]`, that is by the rotations
`t ↦ e^{i(θ₀ - θ₁)} t` of the affine coordinate `t = z₀ / z₁`. The element `ξ = (ξ₀, ξ₁)` of its
Lie algebra `ℝ²` generates the vector field `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R`, where

`R = i t ∂_t` (`OnePoint.rotationVectorField`)

is the infinitesimal rotation; it vanishes at the two fixed points `0` and `∞`.

The **height** of the sphere is the first diagonal entry of the orthogonal projector onto the line
`[z₀ : z₁]` (`TauCeti.hermitianProjector`),

`h([z₀ : z₁]) = |z₀|² / (|z₀|² + |z₁|²)`, that is `h(t) = |t|² / (1 + |t|²)` and `h(∞) = 1`

(`OnePoint.fubiniStudyHeight`). It is smooth (`OnePoint.contMDiff_fubiniStudyHeight`), its image
is `[0, 1]` (`OnePoint.range_fubiniStudyHeight`), and its critical points are exactly the fixed
points `0` and `∞` of the rotation (`OnePoint.mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_eq_zero_iff`).

With the convention `ι_{X_f} σ = df`, the rotation field is the Hamiltonian vector field of the
height for the symplectic form `σ = -2π ω_FS`, where `ω_FS` is the Fubini–Study form of total area
one (`OnePoint.isHamiltonianVectorField_rotationVectorField`). In the affine coordinate both sides
are `2 ⟪t, v⟫ / (1 + |t|²)²` on a tangent vector `v`; at `∞` both vanish. This fixes the
normalization: in the coordinate `w = 1 / t` near `∞` the height is `1 - |w|² + O(|w|⁴)` and the
first circle factor acts on `w` with weight `-1`, so `σ(∂_x, ∂_y) = -2` at `∞`, where `ω_FS` takes
the value `1 / π`.

Consequently the projector diagonal

`μ([z₀ : z₁]) = (|z₀|², |z₁|²) / (|z₀|² + |z₁|²) = (h, 1 - h)`,

read as the linear form `ξ ↦ h ξ₀ + (1 - h) ξ₁` on `ℝ²` (`OnePoint.fubiniStudyMoment`), is a
moment map of the diagonal torus action for `σ = -2π ω_FS`
(`OnePoint.isMomentMap_fubiniStudyMoment`). The infinitesimal action is the one generated by `μ`
as a comoment map (`OnePoint.fubiniStudyTorusAction`), and it sends `ξ` to `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R`
(`OnePoint.fubiniStudyTorusAction_apply`); in particular the rotation field is smooth
(`OnePoint.contMDiff_rotationVectorField`). The coordinate sum of `μ` is the rank `1` of the line,
its values at the fixed points `∞ = [1 : 0]` and `0 = [0 : 1]` are the coordinate vectors
`(1, 0)` and `(0, 1)`, and since `h` takes every value in `[0, 1]` the image of `μ` is the segment
joining them.

The Lie algebra `ℝ² = Fin 2 → ℝ` of the torus carries the commutator bracket of the commutative
algebra `Fin 2 → ℝ` (`LieRing.ofAssociativeRing`), which vanishes. As for
`TauCeti.InfinitesimalAction.linear`, this is a local instance, which a consumer of
`OnePoint.fubiniStudyTorusAction` activates in the same way.

## Main definitions

* `OnePoint.rotationVectorField`: the infinitesimal rotation `i t ∂_t` of the Riemann sphere.
* `OnePoint.fubiniStudyHeight`: the height `|t|² / (1 + |t|²)`, equal to `1` at `∞`.
* `OnePoint.fubiniStudyMoment`: the projector diagonal `ξ ↦ h ξ₀ + (1 - h) ξ₁`.
* `OnePoint.fubiniStudyTorusAction`: the infinitesimal action of the diagonal torus.

## Main results

* `OnePoint.isHamiltonianVectorField_rotationVectorField`: the rotation field is the Hamiltonian
  vector field of the height for `-2π ω_FS`.
* `OnePoint.isMomentMap_fubiniStudyMoment`: the projector diagonal is a moment map of the diagonal
  torus action for `-2π ω_FS`.
* `OnePoint.range_fubiniStudyHeight`, `OnePoint.mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_eq_zero_iff`: the image
  of the height and its critical points.

## References

* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Lecture 22 and Section 27.1 (the moment map of the torus action on complex
  projective space).
* V. Guillemin and S. Sternberg, *Convexity properties of the moment mapping*, Invent. Math. 67
  (1982), 491–513 (the diagonal of the projector as the moment map on coadjoint orbits).
-/

public section

open Set Filter ComplexConjugate TauCeti Projectivization
open scoped Manifold Topology ContDiff InnerProductSpace TauCeti.ComplexManifold

noncomputable section

namespace OnePoint

/-! ### The infinitesimal rotation -/

/-- The **infinitesimal rotation** `R = i t ∂_t` of the Riemann sphere, the generator of the
rotations `t ↦ e^{iθ} t`. A tangent vector is read in the preferred chart of its base point, so `R`
is `i t` at a finite point `t`, and it vanishes at `∞`, where it reads `-i w ∂_w` in the inverted
coordinate `w = 1 / t`. -/
def rotationVectorField (x : OnePoint ℂ) : TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) x :=
  Complex.I * affineChart x

@[simp]
theorem rotationVectorField_coe (z : ℂ) : rotationVectorField z = Complex.I * z := by
  rw [rotationVectorField, affineChart_coe]

@[simp]
theorem rotationVectorField_infty : rotationVectorField ∞ = 0 := by
  rw [rotationVectorField, affineChart_infty, mul_zero]
  -- The tangent space at `∞` is `ℂ`, and its zero is the zero of `ℂ`.
  rfl

/-- The infinitesimal rotation vanishes exactly at its two fixed points `0` and `∞`. -/
theorem rotationVectorField_eq_zero_iff {x : OnePoint ℂ} :
    rotationVectorField x = 0 ↔ x = (0 : ℂ) ∨ x = (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) := by
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => simp
  | coe z =>
    rw [rotationVectorField_coe]
    simp only [OnePoint.coe_ne_infty, or_false, OnePoint.coe_eq_coe]
    exact mul_eq_zero.trans (or_iff_right Complex.I_ne_zero)

/-! ### The height -/

/-- The **height** of the Riemann sphere: the first diagonal entry of the orthogonal projector
onto the line `[z₀ : z₁]` of `ℂ²` (`TauCeti.hermitianProjector`), that is
`|z₀|² / (|z₀|² + |z₁|²)`. At a finite point `t = [t : 1]` it is `|t|² / (1 + |t|²)`
(`OnePoint.fubiniStudyHeight_coe`), and at `∞ = [1 : 0]` it is `1`. -/
def fubiniStudyHeight (x : OnePoint ℂ) : ℝ :=
  (hermitianProjector (equivProjectivization ℂ x) 0 0).re

/-- The height is the first diagonal entry of the orthogonal projector onto the line. -/
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_def (x : OnePoint ℂ) :
    fubiniStudyHeight x = (hermitianProjector (equivProjectivization ℂ x) 0 0).re :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_coe (z : ℂ) : fubiniStudyHeight z = ‖z‖ ^ 2 / (1 + ‖z‖ ^ 2) := by
  rw [fubiniStudyHeight, equivProjectivization_apply_coe, hermitianProjector_mk _ (by simp),
    rankOneHermitianProjector_apply, star_vec2_one_dotProduct_self,
    RCLike.ofReal_eq_complex_ofReal]
  simp only [Matrix.cons_val_zero, Complex.star_def, Complex.mul_conj, ← Complex.ofReal_div,
    Complex.ofReal_re, Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq]

@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_infty : fubiniStudyHeight ∞ = 1 := by
  simp [fubiniStudyHeight, rankOneHermitianProjector_apply, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]

/-- The second diagonal entry of the orthogonal projector onto the line `[z₀ : z₁]`, that is
`|z₁|² / (|z₀|² + |z₁|²)`, is `1` minus the height: the projector has trace `1`. -/
theorem re_hermitianProjector_one_one (x : OnePoint ℂ) :
    (hermitianProjector (equivProjectivization ℂ x) 1 1).re = 1 - fubiniStudyHeight x := by
  have h := congrArg Complex.re (mem_hermitianProjectorLocus.1
    (hermitianProjector_mem_hermitianProjectorLocus (equivProjectivization ℂ x))).2
  rw [Matrix.trace_fin_two, Complex.add_re, Complex.one_re] at h
  rw [fubiniStudyHeight]
  linarith

/-- The height at a finite point is `1 - (1 + |t|²)⁻¹`. -/
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_coe_eq_one_sub (z : ℂ) :
    fubiniStudyHeight z = 1 - (1 + ‖z‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ := by
  rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- In the inverted coordinate `w = 1 / t` the height is `(1 + |w|²)⁻¹`, including at `w = 0`,
the coordinate of `∞`. -/
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_invChart_symm (w : ℂ) :
    fubiniStudyHeight (invChart.symm w) = (1 + ‖w‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ := by
  rcases eq_or_ne w 0 with rfl | hw
  · simp [invChart_symm_zero]
  · rw [invChart_symm_of_ne_zero hw, fubiniStudyHeight_coe, norm_inv, inv_pow]
    field_simp
    ring

theorem fubiniStudyHeight_nonneg (x : OnePoint ℂ) : 0 ≤ fubiniStudyHeight x := by
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => simp
  | coe z => rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe]; positivity

theorem fubiniStudyHeight_le_one (x : OnePoint ℂ) : fubiniStudyHeight x ≤ 1 := by
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => simp
  | coe z => rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe, div_le_one (by positivity)]; linarith

/-- **The image of the height** is the interval `[0, 1]`: the point `[√(s / (1 - s)) : 1]` has
height `s` for `0 ≤ s < 1`, and `∞` has height `1`. -/
theorem range_fubiniStudyHeight : range fubiniStudyHeight = Icc 0 1 := by
  refine Subset.antisymm (range_subset_iff.2 fun x ↦
    ⟨fubiniStudyHeight_nonneg x, fubiniStudyHeight_le_one x⟩) fun s ⟨hs₀, hs₁⟩ ↦ ?_
  rcases hs₁.lt_or_eq with hs₁ | rfl
  · have hpos : 0 < 1 - s := sub_pos.2 hs₁
    refine ⟨((√(s / (1 - s)) : ℝ) : ℂ), ?_⟩
    rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_of_nonneg (Real.sqrt_nonneg _),
      Real.sq_sqrt (div_nonneg hs₀ hpos.le)]
    field_simp
    ring
  · exact ⟨∞, fubiniStudyHeight_infty⟩

/-- The height vanishes only at `0`, its minimum. -/
@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_eq_zero_iff {x : OnePoint ℂ} : fubiniStudyHeight x = 0 ↔ x = (0 : ℂ) := by
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => simp
  | coe z =>
    rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe, div_eq_zero_iff, or_iff_left (by positivity)]
    simp

/-- The height equals `1` only at `∞`, its maximum. -/
@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyHeight_eq_one_iff {x : OnePoint ℂ} :
    fubiniStudyHeight x = 1 ↔ x = (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) := by
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => simp
  | coe z =>
    rw [fubiniStudyHeight_coe, div_eq_one_iff_eq (by positivity)]
    simp

/-! ### Smoothness and the differential of the height -/

/-- The height read in the affine chart at a finite point. -/
private theorem fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_coe_symm (z : ℂ) :
    fubiniStudyHeight ∘ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (z : OnePoint ℂ)).symm =
      fun t ↦ 1 - (1 + ‖t‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ := by
  funext t
  simp [-fubiniStudyHeight_coe, chartAt_coe, affineChart_symm_apply,
    fubiniStudyHeight_coe_eq_one_sub]

/-- The height read in the inverted chart at `∞`. -/
private theorem fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_infty_symm :
    fubiniStudyHeight ∘ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (∞ : OnePoint ℂ)).symm =
      fun w ↦ (1 + ‖w‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ := by
  funext w
  simp [chartAt_infty, fubiniStudyHeight_invChart_symm]

/-- **The height is smooth** on the Riemann sphere: it is `1 - (1 + |t|²)⁻¹` in the affine
coordinate and `(1 + |w|²)⁻¹` in the inverted coordinate. -/
theorem contMDiff_fubiniStudyHeight {n : WithTop ℕ∞} :
    ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) 𝓘(ℝ) n fubiniStudyHeight := by
  -- `t ↦ (1 + |t|²)⁻¹` is the bracket power of exponent `-1`.
  have h : ContDiff ℝ n fun t : ℂ ↦ (1 + ‖t‖ ^ 2)⁻¹ := by
    simpa [Real.rpow_neg_one] using contDiff_one_add_norm_sq_rpow (E := ℂ) (-1) (n := n)
  intro x
  rw [contMDiffAt_iff_contDiffAt_comp_extChartAt_symm]
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty =>
    rw [fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_infty_symm]
    exact h.contDiffAt
  | coe z =>
    rw [fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_coe_symm]
    exact (contDiff_const.sub h).contDiffAt

/-- The differential of the height at a finite point `z`: `dh(v) = 2 ⟪z, v⟫ / (1 + |z|²)²`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_coe (z v : ℂ) :
    mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) fubiniStudyHeight z v = 2 * ⟪z, v⟫_ℝ / (1 + ‖z‖ ^ 2) ^ 2 := by
  have hz : extChartAt 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (z : OnePoint ℂ) z = z := by simp [chartAt_coe, affineChart_coe]
  have hd : fderiv ℝ (fun t : ℂ ↦ 1 - (1 + ‖t‖ ^ 2)⁻¹) z v =
      2 * ⟪z, v⟫_ℝ / (1 + ‖z‖ ^ 2) ^ 2 := by
    have h := (hasStrictFDerivAt_one_add_norm_sq_rpow (-1) z).hasFDerivAt.const_sub 1
    rw [show (-1 : ℝ) - 1 = -2 by norm_num, Real.rpow_neg (by positivity), Real.rpow_two] at h
    simp only [Real.rpow_neg_one] at h
    rw [h.fderiv]
    simp only [neg_apply, smul_apply, innerSL_apply_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  rw [TauCeti.mvfderiv_eq_fderiv_comp_extChartAt_symm, fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_coe_symm,
    hz]
  -- A tangent vector at `z` is read in the affine chart as the complex number `v`.
  exact hd

/-- The height has a critical point at `∞`, its maximum. -/
@[simp]
theorem mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_infty :
    mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) fubiniStudyHeight (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) = 0 := by
  have h0 : extChartAt 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) ∞ = 0 := by simp [chartAt_infty, invChart_infty]
  have hd : fderiv ℝ (fun w : ℂ ↦ (1 + ‖w‖ ^ 2)⁻¹) 0 = 0 := by
    simpa [Real.rpow_neg_one] using
      (hasStrictFDerivAt_one_add_norm_sq_rpow (E := ℂ) (-1) 0).hasFDerivAt.fderiv
  rw [TauCeti.mvfderiv_eq_fderiv_comp_extChartAt_symm, fubiniStudyHeight_comp_extChartAt_infty_symm,
    h0]
  -- The differential at `∞` is read in the inverted chart, whose model space is `ℂ`.
  exact hd

/-! ### The Hamiltonian identity -/

/-- The pointwise identity behind `isHamiltonianVectorField_rotationVectorField`, in the affine
coordinate `z`: `-2π ρ(z) Im (conj (i z) v) = 2 ⟪z, v⟫ / (1 + |z|²)²`. -/
private theorem neg_two_pi_mul_fubiniStudyDensity_mul_im (z v : ℂ) :
    -(2 * Real.pi) * (fubiniStudyDensity z * (conj (Complex.I * z) * v).im) =
      2 * ⟪z, v⟫_ℝ / (1 + ‖z‖ ^ 2) ^ 2 := by
  have him : (conj (Complex.I * z) * v).im = -(v * conj z).re := by
    simp only [map_mul, Complex.conj_I, Complex.mul_im, Complex.mul_re, Complex.neg_re,
      Complex.neg_im, Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, Complex.conj_re, Complex.conj_im]
    ring
  rw [him, ← Complex.inner, fubiniStudyDensity_def]
  field_simp

/-- **The infinitesimal rotation is Hamiltonian for `-2π ω_FS`**: with the convention
`ι_{X_f} σ = df`, it is the Hamiltonian vector field of the height `h(t) = |t|² / (1 + |t|²)` for
the symplectic form `σ = -2π ω_FS`, where `ω_FS` is the Fubini–Study form of total area one. -/
theorem isHamiltonianVectorField_rotationVectorField :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).IsHamiltonianVectorField fubiniStudyHeight
      rotationVectorField := by
  refine SmoothTwoForm.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff.2 fun x v ↦ ?_
  rw [SmoothForm.eval₂_smul, smul_eq_mul]
  induction x using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty =>
    rw [rotationVectorField_infty, SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_zero_left,
      mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_infty]
    exact mul_zero _
  | coe z =>
    rw [rotationVectorField_coe]
    -- The tangent vector `v` at `z` is read in the affine chart as a complex number.
    exact (congrArg _ (eval₂_fubiniStudyForm_coe z _ v)).trans
      ((neg_two_pi_mul_fubiniStudyDensity_mul_im z v).trans
        (mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_coe z v).symm)

/-- The form `-2π ω_FS` is symplectic. -/
theorem isSymplectic_neg_two_pi_smul_fubiniStudyForm :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).IsSymplectic :=
  isSymplectic_fubiniStudyForm.smul _ (neg_ne_zero.2 (by positivity))

/-- The Hamiltonian vector field of the height for `-2π ω_FS` is the infinitesimal rotation. -/
@[simp]
theorem hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyHeight :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).hamiltonianVectorField fubiniStudyHeight =
      rotationVectorField :=
  (isSymplectic_neg_two_pi_smul_fubiniStudyForm.isNondegenerate.isHamiltonianVectorField_iff_eq.1
    isHamiltonianVectorField_rotationVectorField).symm

/-- **The critical points of the height** are exactly the fixed points `0` and `∞` of the
rotation, the zeros of its Hamiltonian vector field. -/
theorem mvfderiv_fubiniStudyHeight_eq_zero_iff {x : OnePoint ℂ} :
    mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) fubiniStudyHeight x = 0 ↔ x = (0 : ℂ) ∨ x = (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) := by
  rw [← isSymplectic_neg_two_pi_smul_fubiniStudyForm.isNondegenerate
    |>.hamiltonianVectorField_eq_zero_iff, hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyHeight,
    rotationVectorField_eq_zero_iff]

/-! ### The moment map of the diagonal torus -/

section Torus

/- The Lie algebra `ℝ²` of the diagonal torus carries the commutator bracket of the commutative
algebra `Fin 2 → ℝ`, which vanishes identically. -/
attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

/-- The **projector diagonal** of the Riemann sphere, as a linear form on the Lie algebra `ℝ²` of
the diagonal torus: at `[z₀ : z₁]` it is `ξ ↦ Σᵢ Pᵢᵢ ξᵢ`, where `P` is the orthogonal projector
onto the line `[z₀ : z₁]` of `ℂ²`, that is `ξ ↦ (|z₀|² ξ₀ + |z₁|² ξ₁) / (|z₀|² + |z₁|²)`. In terms
of the height `h` (`OnePoint.fubiniStudyHeight`) it is `ξ ↦ h ξ₀ + (1 - h) ξ₁`
(`OnePoint.fubiniStudyMoment_apply`). -/
def fubiniStudyMoment (x : OnePoint ℂ) : Module.Dual ℝ (Fin 2 → ℝ) :=
  ∑ i, (hermitianProjector (equivProjectivization ℂ x) i i).re • LinearMap.proj i

/-- The projector diagonal is `ξ ↦ Σᵢ Pᵢᵢ ξᵢ`, where `P` is the orthogonal projector onto the
line. -/
theorem fubiniStudyMoment_def (x : OnePoint ℂ) :
    fubiniStudyMoment x =
      ∑ i, (hermitianProjector (equivProjectivization ℂ x) i i).re • LinearMap.proj i :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyMoment_apply (x : OnePoint ℂ) (ξ : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    fubiniStudyMoment x ξ = fubiniStudyHeight x * ξ 0 + (1 - fubiniStudyHeight x) * ξ 1 := by
  simp [fubiniStudyMoment, Fin.sum_univ_two, re_hermitianProjector_one_one, fubiniStudyHeight]

/-- At the fixed point `∞ = [1 : 0]` the projector diagonal is the first coordinate. -/
theorem fubiniStudyMoment_infty : fubiniStudyMoment (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) = LinearMap.proj 0 := by
  ext ξ
  simp

/-- At the fixed point `0 = [0 : 1]` the projector diagonal is the second coordinate. -/
theorem fubiniStudyMoment_zero : fubiniStudyMoment (0 : ℂ) = LinearMap.proj 1 := by
  ext ξ
  simp

/-- The two entries of the projector diagonal sum to `1`, the rank of the line. -/
theorem fubiniStudyMoment_apply_one (x : OnePoint ℂ) : fubiniStudyMoment x 1 = 1 := by
  simp

/-- A component of the projector diagonal is an affine function of the height. -/
private theorem fubiniStudyMoment_component (ξ : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    (fun x ↦ fubiniStudyMoment x ξ) = fun x ↦ ((ξ 0 - ξ 1) • fubiniStudyHeight) x + ξ 1 := by
  funext x
  simp only [fubiniStudyMoment_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
  ring

private theorem contMDiff_fubiniStudyMoment_apply {n : WithTop ℕ∞} (ξ : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) 𝓘(ℝ) n fun x ↦ fubiniStudyMoment x ξ := by
  have hlin : ContDiff ℝ n fun s : ℝ ↦ (ξ 0 - ξ 1) * s + ξ 1 := by fun_prop
  refine (hlin.comp_contMDiff contMDiff_fubiniStudyHeight).congr fun x ↦ ?_
  simp only [Function.comp_apply, fubiniStudyMoment_apply]
  ring

/-- The Hamiltonian vector field of the component `μ_ξ` for `-2π ω_FS` is `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R`. -/
private theorem hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyMoment_apply (ξ : Fin 2 → ℝ) (x : OnePoint ℂ) :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).hamiltonianVectorField
        (fun y ↦ fubiniStudyMoment y ξ) x =
      (ξ 0 - ξ 1) • rotationVectorField x := by
  rw [fubiniStudyMoment_component, SmoothTwoForm.hamiltonianVectorField_add_const,
    SmoothTwoForm.hamiltonianVectorField_const_smul, hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyHeight]

/-- The components of the projector diagonal Poisson-commute, as the torus is abelian. -/
private theorem poissonBracket_fubiniStudyMoment (ξ η : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).poissonBracket (fun x ↦ fubiniStudyMoment x ξ)
      (fun x ↦ fubiniStudyMoment x η) = fun x ↦ fubiniStudyMoment x ⁅ξ, η⁆ := by
  funext x
  -- `ℝ²` is commutative, so the bracket `⁅ξ, η⁆` vanishes, as does `σ(X, X)`.
  rw [(Commute.all ξ η).lie_eq, map_zero]
  simp only [SmoothTwoForm.poissonBracket_def, hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyMoment_apply,
    SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_smul_left, SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_smul_right,
    SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_self, smul_zero]

/-- The **infinitesimal action of the diagonal torus** on the Riemann sphere, generated by the
projector diagonal as a comoment map for `-2π ω_FS`. It sends `ξ ∈ ℝ²` to `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R`
(`OnePoint.fubiniStudyTorusAction_apply`), the generator of
`(θ₀, θ₁) · [z₀ : z₁] = [e^{iθ₀} z₀ : e^{iθ₁} z₁]`. -/
def fubiniStudyTorusAction : InfinitesimalAction (Fin 2 → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ) :=
  isSymplectic_neg_two_pi_smul_fubiniStudyForm.comomentAction fubiniStudyMoment
    contMDiff_fubiniStudyMoment_apply poissonBracket_fubiniStudyMoment

/-- The diagonal torus action sends `ξ` to `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R`, where `R = i t ∂_t` is the infinitesimal
rotation. -/
@[simp]
theorem fubiniStudyTorusAction_apply (ξ : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    fubiniStudyTorusAction ξ = (ξ 0 - ξ 1) • rotationVectorField := by
  funext x
  rw [fubiniStudyTorusAction, SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.comomentAction_apply,
    hamiltonianVectorField_fubiniStudyMoment_apply, Pi.smul_apply]

/-- **The projector diagonal is a moment map** of the diagonal torus action on the Riemann sphere
for the symplectic form `-2π ω_FS`: for every `ξ ∈ ℝ²`, the generator `(ξ₀ - ξ₁) R` is the
Hamiltonian vector field of `x ↦ μ(x)(ξ)`. -/
theorem isMomentMap_fubiniStudyMoment :
    ((-(2 * Real.pi)) • fubiniStudyForm).IsMomentMap fubiniStudyTorusAction fubiniStudyMoment :=
  SmoothTwoForm.IsSymplectic.isMomentMap_comomentAction _ _ _ _

-- The smoothness exponent `((⊤ : ℕ∞) : WithTop ℕ∞)` is the value of the notation `∞` of
-- `ContDiff`, which is ambiguous with the point `∞` inside the namespace `OnePoint`.
/-- **The infinitesimal rotation is smooth**: it is the generator of the element `(1, 0)` of the
diagonal torus action. -/
theorem contMDiff_rotationVectorField :
    ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ).tangent ((⊤ : ℕ∞) : WithTop ℕ∞)
      fun x ↦ (⟨x, rotationVectorField x⟩ : TangentBundle 𝓘(ℝ, ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ)) := by
  have h := fubiniStudyTorusAction.contMDiff (Pi.single 0 1)
  simpa using h

end Torus

end OnePoint
